ctive_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.5.1, 4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - Fedora Linux 42.20251028.0 (Silverblue) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Single-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon 780M Graphics (RADV PHOENIX) - AMD Ryzen 7 7840U w/ Radeon  780M Graphics (16 threads) - 30.64 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIssue: Evaluator does not work when you have a breakpoint inside a static function. It seems to just continue execution.\n\nExpected behavior: I am able to evaluate expressions when I have stopped at a breakpoint inside a static function.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1) have a node with the following script attached:\n```gdscript\nextends Node2D\n\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tprint('Hello')\n\t\n\tmy_func()\n\t\n\tprint('World')\n\n\nstatic func my_func() -> void:\n\tvar i = 15\n\t\n\tprint('eval test')\n```\n2) Add a breakpoint on line with `print('eval test')`, and another one on line with `print('World')`\n3) Run the project\n4) In the debuggers evaluator tab, try to check for the value of `i`\n5) Observe that the value of `i` was not shown, now you are at the stack trace tab in the debugger menu, and the place in the code that you have stopped is in the line's `print('World')` breakpoint\n\nAlternatively you can not put a breakline on `print('World')` and just see that the execution continues and there is now a line with the word 'World' in the output.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.githu